# Env for the crush-signal harness (referenced as env_file in harness.toml).
#
# harness parses this as KEY=VALUE (a leading `export ` and surrounding quotes are
# tolerated) and layers it ON TOP of the daemon's own environment — spawn.go does
# `env := os.Environ()` and appends, so PATH and everything else the daemon already
# has still reaches crush; these entries just win on conflict.
#
# NO SECRETS HERE. This file is committed to the dotfiles repo. Crush's provider key
# ($ZAI_API_TOKEN) and every MCP token come from ~/.config/vault/secrets-static.env,
# which Vault Agent renders from OpenBao and your login shell sources via
# ~/.oh-my-zsh/custom/00-secrets.zsh. Practical consequence: start `harness daemon`
# from a shell that has those sourced. If you ever move the daemon under launchd or
# systemd so it starts at boot without a login shell, point this harness's env_file
# at secrets-static.env instead — harness's parser reads that file's `export K='v'`
# lines correctly — or merge the two.

# Repoint crush's override config (GlobalConfigData) at a per-harness file, so the
# model pin in ~/.local/share/crush-signal/crush.json applies to this supervised
# crush and not to the one you run by hand. Unset, this would be
# ~/.local/share/crush. The dir also holds this agent's session history, so if you
# rename the harness again, `mv` the dir rather than letting a new one be seeded.
CRUSH_GLOBAL_DATA={{ .chezmoi.homeDir }}/.local/share/crush-signal
